## 3. Naming conventions — exact, checkable

| Artefact | Pattern | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Aggregate | `<Noun>` | `User`, `Course`, `Enrollment` |
| Value object | `<Noun>` (record/enum) | `EmailAddress`, `ProfileId`, `EnrollmentStatus` |
| Command | `<Verb><Noun>Command` | `SignUpCommand`, `CreateCourseCommand` |
| Query | `Get<Noun>By<Criterion>Query` / `GetAll<Nouns>Query` | `GetUserByIdQuery` |
| Domain port | `<Aggregate>Repository` | `UserRepository` |
| Inbound port | `<Aggregate>CommandService` / `QueryService` | `UserQueryService` |
| Inbound impl | same name + `Impl`, under `internal` | `UserQueryServiceImpl` |
| Persistence entity | `<Aggregate>PersistenceEntity` | `UserPersistenceEntity` |
| Spring Data repo | `<Aggregate>PersistenceRepository` | `UserPersistenceRepository` |
| Adapter | `<Aggregate>RepositoryImpl` | `UserRepositoryImpl` |
| Persistence assembler | `<Aggregate>PersistenceAssembler` | `UserPersistenceAssembler` |
| VO converter | `<VO>PersistenceConverter` | `EmailAddressPersistenceConverter` |
| VO embeddable | `<VO>PersistenceEmbeddable` | `PersonNamePersistenceEmbeddable` |
| Controller | `<Nouns>Controller` (plural) | `UsersController` |
| REST DTO | `<Noun>Resource`, `Create<Noun>Resource` | `UserResource` |
| REST transform | `<Noun>ResourceFromEntityAssembler` / `<Cmd>CommandFromResourceAssembler` | — |

Deviation from these names is `MINOR` **unless** it hides a structural gap, e.g. a class named `UserService` that is simultaneously the port, the impl, and the repository. That is `MAJOR`.

