## 4. Dependency rules

| From | May import | May NOT import |
|---|---|---|
| `<ctx>.domain` | `java.*`, `org.jspecify`, own domain, `shared.domain` | `application`, `infrastructure`, `interfaces`, any other context |
| `<ctx>.application` | own `domain`, `shared.domain`, `shared.application` | `infrastructure`, `interfaces` of any context except through an ACL facade interface |
| `<ctx>.infrastructure` | own `domain`, own `application` ports, `shared.infrastructure` | `interfaces` |
| `<ctx>.interfaces` | own `application` ports, own `domain` types | `infrastructure`, Spring Data repositories |
| `shared.*` | `java.*`, framework | **any concrete bounded context** (cycle) |
| context A | context B **only** via `B.interfaces.acl.BContextFacade` | any other B package |

### 4.1 HARD INVARIANT

No file under any `domain/` package imports:

- `jakarta.persistence.*`
- `org.springframework.web.*`
- `org.springframework.data.jpa.*`
- `org.springframework.stereotype.*`

Every violation is a `BLOCKER`, reported individually with file and line.

> **Documented exception in the reference:** `shared.domain.model.aggregates.AbstractDomainAggregateRoot` imports `org.springframework.data.domain.AbstractAggregateRoot`. That is Spring Data **Commons**, not JPA, and exists solely for domain-event registration. Do not report it. Report any *other* Spring import in domain.

### 4.2 Additional banned edges

| Package | Banned | Severity | Reason |
|---|---|---|---|
| `domain` | `lombok.Data` | MAJOR | generates setters and `equals` that break aggregate invariants |
| `application` | `jakarta.persistence` | MAJOR | persistence leaked past the port |
| `interfaces` | `*PersistenceEntity` | MAJOR | endpoint bypassing the domain |
| `interfaces` | `*PersistenceRepository` / `JpaRepository` | BLOCKER | endpoint talking to the database |
| `interfaces` | `infrastructure.*` | BLOCKER | inverted dependency |
| any context | another context's `domain`/`application` | BLOCKER | broken context boundary |

