## 9. Refactor branch plan

Constraints: **one concern per branch**; each branch compiles and boots at its tip; Conventional Commits; no branch mixes a move with a behaviour change. A rename and a logic change in one commit make the diff unreadable and the revert impossible.

| # | Branch | Content | Done when |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | `chore/audit-baseline` | Commit the audit report only. No source changes. Fixes the reference point every later branch is measured against. | Report is on the default branch |
| 1 | `refactor/domain-purity` | Remove every banned import from `domain/`. Move JPA annotations onto persistence entities. Introduce `AbstractDomainAggregateRoot` if absent. **No behaviour change.** | Grep for §4.1 imports under `domain/` returns nothing; app boots |
| 2 | `refactor/persistence-entities` | Split each dual-purpose class into a plain aggregate and an `XPersistenceEntity` extending the auditable base. | Every aggregate has a matching persistence entity; DDL is unchanged, verified by diffing generated schema |
| 3 | `refactor/repository-ports` | Introduce `domain/repositories` interfaces expressed in domain types. Existing Spring Data interfaces renamed to `XPersistenceRepository`. No method bodies rewritten. | No class outside `infrastructure` names a `JpaRepository` |
| 4 | `refactor/persistence-adapters` | Add `XRepositoryImpl` implementing each port and delegating. | No class outside `adapters` names both a domain type and a persistence entity |
| 5 | `refactor/assemblers` | Create missing assemblers; close every field-coverage gap from §E. **Highest defect risk — this branch does nothing else.** | Every field of both targets assigned in both directions, verified field by field, collections included |
| 6 | `refactor/split-command-query` | Break the `services` catch-all into `application/commandservices` + `application/queryservices` ports and `application/internal/...` impls. Pure moves and renames. | Every service sits in exactly one of the four folders |
| 7 | `refactor/commands-and-queries` | Move command and query records from `internal` into `domain/model/commands` and `domain/model/queries`. | `internal` contains only `@Service` implementations, event handlers, and outbound services |
| 8 | `refactor/rest-transform` | Add missing `resources` records and `transform` assemblers; stop controllers touching entities. | No controller names a persistence entity |
| 9 | `refactor/shared-extraction` | Pull single-consumer members out of `shared`; move any misplaced infrastructure base class out of `shared/domain`. | Every remaining `shared` member has at least two consumers |
| 10 | `refactor/context-acl` | Replace direct cross-context imports with `interfaces/acl` facades plus `outboundservices/acl` callers. | Every cross-context import targets an `acl` package |
| 11 | `fix/transactions` | Correct `@Transactional` placement, self-invocation, and any failure path that returns instead of throwing. | Each write path's rollback behaviour is stated and tested manually |
| 12 | `chore/naming-conformance` | All `MINOR` renames and placements, batched. Zero logic change. | Layout matches §2 and §3 |
| 13 | `build/annotation-processing` | Only if §J found defects: single compiler plugin block, exhaustive processor paths. | Clean build log shows the processor ran |
| 14 | `test/architecture-rules` | ArchUnit rules for §4.1 and the §4 table. Written last, so it locks a state that already holds. | Rules pass on the default branch |

**Merge discipline**

- Branches 1 → 5 are strictly sequential; each depends on its predecessor.
- Branches 6 → 10 may run in parallel with one another once 5 lands.
- Branch 14 must be last, or it fails on arrival and gets weakened until it passes, which is worse than not having it.
- Rebase within a branch rather than merge-committing, so each step stays one readable diff.

**Rollback rule:** if a branch cannot be reverted cleanly, it did more than one thing. Split it.